            <ArticleTitle>Shearing of the plastic coating of a hydrophilic guide wire in a right femoropopliteal bypass graft: removal from the contralateral side.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The plastic coating of a hydrophilic guide wire tore off during introduction through a beveled single wall arterial entry needle in a 75 year old male. The sheared piece of coating got stuck in his femoropopliteal bypass. It was removed by means of a modified arterial filter set from the contralateral side. The technique of its removal is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
